WEBVTT

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:07.900
<i>No. 4 Division just barely 
managed to protect Annex 1.</i>

00:00:09.640 --> 00:00:12.860
<i>Their leader, Liu, hurried 
to capture the targets.</i>

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:21.360
<i>A missile was fired at Akari and Michelle 
as they battled the terraformars.</i>

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:26.580
<i>As things looked bleakest, Akari was given...</i>

00:00:28.100 --> 00:00:33.470
<i>...the anti-terraformar vibro-ninja-blade, 
sent by Alexander.</i>

00:00:44.090 --> 00:00:46.270
I'm Minamoto Yuriko.

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.400
I'll be living here with you starting today.

00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:52.150
Who are you?

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:01.620
I'm Harukaze Sakurato.

00:01:02.110 --> 00:01:03.160
I'm ten!

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:06.500
I'm staying in that hospital.

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:09.290
That's a really neat name.

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:10.460
What about you?

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:19.450
<b>Hizamaru</b>

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:18.830
Hizamaru!

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:26.140
Hizamaru Shingan Style.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:32.180
I was abandoned in front of a 
dojo with that name on the door.

00:01:33.270 --> 00:01:40.360
The letter was written in English, 
Japanese, French... every language.

00:01:40.690 --> 00:01:42.460
It said the same thing in each language.

00:01:42.840 --> 00:01:46.500
"Please take care of this child. His name is..."

00:01:47.420 --> 00:01:50.840
The name was different in each language, 
but they all meant the same thing.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.590
"A blazing torch."

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:57.100
Why am I telling you this?

00:01:58.230 --> 00:02:00.510
Sorry for buying time.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:04.320
I am Hizamaru Akari, master 
of the Hizamaru Shingan Style!

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:07.980
Let us do battle!

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.890
<b><i>The First Day</i></b>

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:45.760
They're still howling...

00:03:48.270 --> 00:03:50.220
Until they stop moving...

00:03:50.220 --> 00:03:51.410
Kill them.

00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.490
Kill them all!

00:03:55.070 --> 00:03:57.480
Kill them, no matter what.

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:03.940
The sort of burning hatred that 
humanity bears only for cockroaches,

00:04:03.940 --> 00:04:07.570
as well as an incredible rate of evolution.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:11.690
There's a theory that 
these were the artificial

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:14.690
creations of a certain ancient civilization.

00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:17.730
The name of the civilization is Rahab.

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.640
There are references to

00:04:19.640 --> 00:04:22.990
the name in human writing that 
call it the "Home of the Demons".

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:26.700
And this theory says that there was actually 
a planet between Mars and Jupiter.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:32.140
They possessed a means of interstellar 
travel and, in addition to Mars,

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:34.970
they also flew to Venus, the Moon,

00:04:35.510 --> 00:04:40.630
Europa, and the Earth, and 
left traces of their presence.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.230
I thought it was just one of 
those crazy conspiracy theories.

00:04:46.620 --> 00:04:50.860
But over the past few decades, 
it's started to look real,

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:54.510
because we've seen things 
on Mars that can only be

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:57.400
explained by the use of unknown technology.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:02.360
The Mars ruins and the incredible rate 
of evolution the terraformars possess...

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:04.980
The theory says that there

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:07.960
is probably something somewhere 
on Mars that controls evolution.

00:05:07.960 --> 00:05:10.280
And if anyone could make such 
a thing, it would be Rahab,

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:13.620
a civilization so powerful it 
was once thought of as a god.

00:05:14.740 --> 00:05:17.310
The man behind the B.U.G.S. operation,

00:05:17.310 --> 00:05:21.250
Commander Alexander Gustav Newton, 
came up with that hypothesis

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:25.370
and the Russian president, 
Smiles, quietly supported him.

00:05:26.030 --> 00:05:32.260
So our job is to either find 
that device and stop the war,

00:05:32.260 --> 00:05:36.900
or steal it so that humanity 
can become even more powerful.

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:42.040
One of the two... and of course, 
the latter would be best.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:46.450
So that's why No. 3 Division 
examined the pyramids,

00:05:47.520 --> 00:05:50.710
and we found our hypothesis was wrong.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.240
Nothing that convenient actually exists.

00:05:54.500 --> 00:05:58.960
Humans has destroyed and stolen from 
many civilizations in our history.

00:05:59.830 --> 00:06:02.540
But this time, we can't destroy.

00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:03.770
We can't steal.

00:06:03.770 --> 00:06:07.260
Because it's already been destroyed!

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.800
This planet was made from 
a single miscalculation,

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:18.230
and the tragedy of those who 
were left behind with nothing.

00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:26.650
<i>I see...</i>

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:31.100
<i>So that's why I wanted to give him 
my name when he can't even speak.</i>

00:06:31.700 --> 00:06:33.190
<i>Wow...</i>

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.660
<i>These guys are warriors!</i>

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:39.730
<i>They probably practiced without rest...</i>

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:44.040
<i>in order to defeat us, despite not 
knowing when we would come.</i>

00:06:44.680 --> 00:06:45.960
<i>Wow.</i>

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:08.830
I am Hizamaru.

00:07:10.000 --> 00:07:11.780
Hizamaru Akari.

00:07:13.220 --> 00:07:15.230
What a cool name.

00:07:15.230 --> 00:07:16.330
Hizamaru-san!

00:07:17.470 --> 00:07:21.320
I know you have something you want 
even if it means you have to kill me.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.340
But I can't afford to lose anything else.

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:29.210
So whoever wins, no hard feelings.

00:07:41.130 --> 00:07:44.550
I need to get to Michelle-san...

00:07:46.230 --> 00:07:52.060
She's probably fighting right now!

00:07:57.990 --> 00:07:59.250
<i>That hurt.</i>

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.000
Michelle!

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.670
Is it okay for you to be up?

00:08:09.090 --> 00:08:11.630
Mom, did you hear?

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:13.340
Yeah, I did.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.010
The police said it was 
probably a gas explosion.

00:08:16.630 --> 00:08:20.940
All your friends have broken
 their bones in several places,

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.270
and still aren't up for talking.

00:08:24.940 --> 00:08:27.010
I know I shouldn't say this,

00:08:27.010 --> 00:08:29.360
but you're lucky.

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.770
<i>No, Mom.</i>

00:08:32.340 --> 00:08:35.730
<i>It wasn't that I was lucky enough 
not to have any rubble fall on me.</i>

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:38.160
<i>That wasn't what happened.</i>

00:08:38.860 --> 00:08:42.870
<i>That was the day, when I was 
only thirteen, that I learned</i>

00:08:42.870 --> 00:08:46.790
<i>I couldn't live as a normal girl anymore.</i>

00:08:48.630 --> 00:08:50.090
<i>I hated it.</i>

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:51.970
<i>I hated it.</i>

00:08:53.140 --> 00:08:55.250
<i>I hated that power so much.</i>

00:08:55.750 --> 00:09:00.810
Your father was one of the 
finest men I ever met.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:04.580
He sacrificed his life to protect us.

00:09:06.510 --> 00:09:08.550
I didn't expect this result,

00:09:09.070 --> 00:09:11.570
but I'd imagine that you 
suspected this on some level.

00:09:12.430 --> 00:09:16.310
We've learned that his power 
has been passed down to you.

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:20.780
He was always worried about you.

00:09:20.780 --> 00:09:22.150
This isn't an easy job,

00:09:22.150 --> 00:09:26.630
but I'm sure he'd be happy if 
he knew you'd come to see him.

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.380
Go see him.

00:09:29.800 --> 00:09:32.350
Welcome to the Mars Exploration team.

00:09:32.350 --> 00:09:36.760
And happy twenty-second birthday, Michelle.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:44.080
<i>All I knew about my father was</i>

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:48.440
<i>that something classified had happened 
on Mars and resulted in his death.</i>

00:09:49.190 --> 00:09:55.110
<i>I even suspected he might 
have actually abandoned me.</i>

00:09:56.080 --> 00:10:01.620
<i>Because I had this devil 
inside me, I thought...</i>

00:10:03.190 --> 00:10:04.280
<i>But...</i>

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:12.800
Did you know, Michelle?

00:10:13.430 --> 00:10:18.880
Ants are the strongest of all insects.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:20.530
Are they?

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:22.720
Wow, ants are amazing, Daddy!

00:10:25.600 --> 00:10:30.000
<i>What I thought was the power of a 
devil was actually my father's power.</i>

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:34.610
<i>I was always being protected 
by the power of my father,</i>

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:37.360
<i>which I never should have received.</i>

00:10:38.500 --> 00:10:41.180
<i>Thank you, Daddy.</i>

00:10:49.700 --> 00:10:54.470
<i>I wondered why Dad was so into ants.</i>

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:58.020
But now I can tell.

00:10:58.470 --> 00:11:02.930
They're a lot stronger than this.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:05.310
Ants are the strongest!

00:11:05.310 --> 00:11:07.640
They're a lot stronger than this!

00:11:07.640 --> 00:11:12.600
<i>The power my father left to protect 
me is a lot stronger than this!</i>

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:20.730
<i>I've found it, Paraponera.</i>

00:11:21.330 --> 00:11:23.040
<i>The reason I can't die,</i>

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:28.540
<i>and the reason I have to 
settle things with you here.</i>

00:11:28.540 --> 00:11:30.000
<i>Not for anyone else...</i>

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:35.260
<i>but so I myself can reclaim my human life.</i>

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.320
Unique Weapon: Anti-Terraformar Detonator-Type
 Pure Acceleration Device, Michael's Hammer

00:11:36.150 --> 00:11:37.610
I'll defeat you.

00:11:39.450 --> 00:11:40.800
Now...

00:11:41.650 --> 00:11:43.960
<b>Michelle K. Davis
Surgery Base: Camponotus saundersi + Paraponera
M.A.R.S. Ranking #5</b>

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:43.500
stand.

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.980
<b>Anti-Terraformar Vibro-Ninja-Blade Hizamaru
The unique weapon of #6, Hizamaru Akari.
 It contains many features that allow it to match the bagworm moth,
 such as the ability to emit supersonic waves and wind up thread.</b>

00:11:46.010 --> 00:11:49.980
<b>Anti-Terraformar Detonator-Type Pure Acceleration Device
Michael's Hammer
The Unique Weapon of #5, Michelle K. Davis.
It uses accelerators placed on the elbows, heels, 
and back to drastically increase speed and attack power. 
A normal human's sense of balance and kinetic vision wouldn't
 be able to keep up with it, so they wouldn't be able to move at all.</b>

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:52.730
Pray.

00:11:53.200 --> 00:11:56.000
And if you do have a culture 
that prays, know this.

00:11:56.900 --> 00:11:59.170
Desecration of a corpse

00:12:00.780 --> 00:12:02.910
enrages your foes more than anything else.

00:12:28.710 --> 00:12:29.720
What's wrong?

00:12:30.270 --> 00:12:31.180
Stand up.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:00.340
<i>I knew this.</i>

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:05.840
<i>My father didn't want revenge.</i>

00:13:08.100 --> 00:13:11.260
<i>Even if I defeated the ones who stole his body,</i>

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.570
<i>he wasn't coming back.</i>

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:19.120
<i>I know all that.</i>

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:26.240
<i>But then, what about my soul?</i>

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:31.300
<i>I'm never going to live a normal life.</i>

00:13:31.300 --> 00:13:32.370
<i>So what about my soul?</i>

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:37.570
<i>My weight is over 80 kilograms.</i>

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:40.980
<i>I can hear sounds that other people can't.</i>

00:13:41.720 --> 00:13:44.080
<i>Sometimes I grow horns.</i>

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:47.180
<i>Who could I talk to about that?</i>

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:51.800
<i>Who could I share my heart with?</i>

00:13:52.390 --> 00:13:54.960
<i>That's why I ended up alone.</i>

00:13:55.860 --> 00:13:59.090
<i>But even if I'd pretended 
to forget about my body</i>

00:13:59.090 --> 00:14:02.210
<i>and about my father's 
death, even after wanting</i>

00:14:03.060 --> 00:14:05.670
<i>to learn the truth so badly,</i>

00:14:05.670 --> 00:14:07.980
<i>and pretended to live a normal life...</i>

00:14:09.110 --> 00:14:11.280
<i>What would become of my soul?!</i>

00:14:12.710 --> 00:14:15.160
So now you've used the Paraponera's weapons!

00:14:17.750 --> 00:14:18.960
What?

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:21.540
Did it look like I was in 
that much danger, Alex?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:24.510
Well, if you're in danger, I'll help you.

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:27.080
You're a good fighter,

00:14:27.080 --> 00:14:28.810
and a good commander,

00:14:29.300 --> 00:14:31.470
and a pretty girl.

00:14:31.900 --> 00:14:34.860
But if you get any closer,

00:14:34.860 --> 00:14:36.930
I won't be able to fire accurately.

00:14:37.410 --> 00:14:38.900
That's okay, right?

00:14:38.900 --> 00:14:42.990
If you want to settle things yourself, 
like we originally planned,

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:45.900
I'll believe in you.

00:14:49.570 --> 00:14:50.890
This is the last one.

00:14:51.390 --> 00:14:53.410
Let's finish this!

00:14:53.770 --> 00:14:55.870
<i>I'm not alone anymore...</i>

00:14:55.870 --> 00:14:59.040
<i>In my destiny...!</i>

00:15:15.200 --> 00:15:17.880
<i>It hurts...</i>

00:15:19.780 --> 00:15:20.980
<i>Forward!</i>

00:15:21.780 --> 00:15:22.650
<i>Forward!</i>

00:15:23.320 --> 00:15:24.610
<i>Forward!</i>

00:15:25.200 --> 00:15:26.570
<i>I don't want to run!</i>

00:15:26.570 --> 00:15:27.820
<i>I don't want to lose!</i>

00:15:28.670 --> 00:15:31.860
<i>This isn't what Dad wants...</i>

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:34.810
<i>But because I couldn't lie...</i>

00:15:35.640 --> 00:15:37.570
<i>This is my only choice!</i>

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:47.850
<i>Yaeko and Alex didn't say anything
 and followed the plan!</i>

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:51.400
Fire that second goddamn missile!

00:15:52.580 --> 00:15:56.720
<i>When Akari realized we were 
fighting the Paraponera,</i>

00:15:56.720 --> 00:15:58.800
<i>he jumped right in.</i>

00:15:59.440 --> 00:16:02.980
<i>They all did that for me.</i>

00:16:06.240 --> 00:16:07.680
<i>Right?</i>

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:12.190
<i>I really can't let them get away with this!</i>

00:16:18.360 --> 00:16:21.160
<i>Akari, remember what you said?</i>

00:16:22.750 --> 00:16:25.000
We will put an end to the 
source of this sadness!

00:16:26.890 --> 00:16:28.530
<i>Bye-bye, Paraponera!</i>

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.510
<i>I'm continuing my mission!</i>

00:17:06.860 --> 00:17:10.110
I can't move another step.

00:17:10.750 --> 00:17:13.300
Can I just call it a day?

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:19.400
You capture them for me.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:22.600
I'm bad at that.

00:17:42.450 --> 00:17:44.910
<i>Thank you, Akari.</i>

00:17:46.070 --> 00:17:50.540
You're seeking vengeance because 
you need to do this for yourself.

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:55.380
It's not about whether Yuriko 
or your dad comes back.

00:17:56.060 --> 00:18:01.810
In order to fight this insane 
disaster that threatens our lives,

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.590
we will put an end to the 
source of this sadness!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:13.720
I'm... here...

00:18:13.720 --> 00:18:15.810
Welcome back.

00:18:17.050 --> 00:18:20.070
That's another really embarrassing entrance.

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:30.880
Oww.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.400
Well done, Akari.

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.490
You, too, Michelle.

00:18:40.670 --> 00:18:42.060
We did it, huh?

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:48.350
Put an end to the source of this sadness?

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:52.360
Pretty cool line, for a kid.

00:18:53.190 --> 00:18:57.240
But once this fight is over,

00:18:57.240 --> 00:19:01.320
I want you to think about 
living a normal life.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:05.020
I'm sure it'll be great fun.

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:14.210
Wh-What?

00:19:15.170 --> 00:19:16.640
No...

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:20.460
I was just remembering all that 
selfish crap you said to me.

00:19:21.080 --> 00:19:25.820
I mean, a normal life? After all this?

00:19:25.820 --> 00:19:27.830
I'm already twenty-four,

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:29.950
and I've dedicated my whole life to my work.

00:19:29.950 --> 00:19:31.260
It's too late for that.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:35.740
Oh, it's fine. You can do it, Michelle-san.

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:38.650
And you're not twenty-four anymore.

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:44.400
Your birthday's April 19th, right?

00:19:44.850 --> 00:19:46.970
That's today, I think.

00:19:47.490 --> 00:19:49.830
Counting from the time we arrived on Mars.

00:19:51.960 --> 00:19:54.100
You're right. It's today.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.040
Right?

00:19:55.550 --> 00:19:57.220
I see.

00:19:57.220 --> 00:19:58.940
Twenty-five, huh?

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:01.240
Well, it's a nice round number.

00:20:03.310 --> 00:20:06.010
Add five years and you'll be thirty.

00:20:06.550 --> 00:20:08.370
Why would you add five years?

00:20:08.370 --> 00:20:12.770
Oh, um... Sorry.

00:20:12.770 --> 00:20:13.780
You wouldn't.

00:20:15.630 --> 00:20:20.440
<i>To be honest, I was worried about what 
kind of scum I'd be expected to work with.</i>

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:23.630
<i>They were a crew that had 
given up on a normal life,</i>

00:20:23.630 --> 00:20:26.020
<i>and come to undergo human experimentation.</i>

00:20:26.800 --> 00:20:29.750
<i>But I was wrong, Dad.</i>

00:20:30.350 --> 00:20:32.830
<i>This probably wasn't what you wanted.</i>

00:20:33.450 --> 00:20:36.570
<i>But I came here anyway,</i>

00:20:36.570 --> 00:20:39.360
<i>and, in the end, 
I was blessed with comrades.</i>

00:20:39.850 --> 00:20:46.390
<i>Now my goal in life is to lead 
them, and fight with them.</i>

00:20:46.990 --> 00:20:50.060
Happy birthday.

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:53.170
Yeah... Thank you.

00:20:54.940 --> 00:21:01.730
<i>Give me just a little more time until 
I solve the Mars virus problem, Dad.</i>

00:21:05.380 --> 00:21:06.720
Let's hurry.

00:21:06.720 --> 00:21:08.880
I'm worried about Captain 
Komachi and the others.

00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:12.590
We didn't expect this fight to be so hard.

00:21:12.590 --> 00:21:16.360
But now we have to go get No. 
6 Division, no matter what.

00:21:17.460 --> 00:21:19.270
Can you move, Akari?

00:21:19.270 --> 00:21:20.380
I don't know.

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:24.780
I didn't expect to break so many bones.

00:21:25.590 --> 00:21:29.220
I'm worried about why No. 4 
Division only fired one missile.

00:21:31.270 --> 00:21:35.100
We need Alex and Yaeko to pick us up.

00:21:35.460 --> 00:21:37.120
